session Grounding_Base = Discrete_Planning_Common +
  description \<open>Stable, Analysis-free base for the PDDL pipeline: the Formal-PDDL-Semantics
    Discrete_Planning_Common Abstract_Syntax + the propositional-logic library + assorted HOL-Library/Show
    theories, re-elaborated ONCE on top of the cached Discrete_Planning_Common heap. Discrete_Planning_Common is
    the discrete, HOL-Analysis/ODE-free core of the PDDL semantics, so this base -- and the whole
    reusable Grounding_Common spine above it -- is free of the heavy euclidean/ODE tower. Only the
    classical base (Grounding_Classical_Base) pulls the continuous tower, by importing Classical_Planning.
    Does NOT depend on Temporal_Planning or Classical_Planning, so editing the temporal/classical PDDL
    semantics in Formal-PDDL-Semantics does not invalidate it. SAT-free and graph-free. Contains no
    project-local theories.\<close>
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
    "Show"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems"
  theories [document = false]
    "HOL-Library.Sublist"
    "HOL-Library.List_Lexorder"
    "HOL-Library.Char_ord"
    "HOL-Library.Monad_Syntax"
    "Show.Show_Instances"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems.Sema"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems.CNF"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems.CNF_Formulas"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems.CNF_Sema"
    "Propositional_Proof_Systems.CNF_Formulas_Sema"
    "Discrete_Planning_Common.Abstract_Syntax"
